  "worked_solution": "First, we need to convert $350g=0.350kg$\n\nThe $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{x-\\overset{\u2015}{x}}{\\sigma }.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set.\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=3$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{x-\\overset{\u00af}{x}}{\\sigma } \\\\  & =\\frac{3-3.2}{0.350} \\\\  & =-0.57\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nto $2$ decimal places.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
